1
00:00:00,810 --> 00:00:03,070
Your computer can't
actually do anything.

2
00:00:03,890 --> 00:00:04,790
Not the way you think.

3
00:00:05,570 --> 00:00:09,250
Every photo, song and game
on it comes down to one

4
00:00:09,250 --> 00:00:12,370
tiny trick, repeated
over and over.

5
00:00:13,070 --> 00:00:16,050
Inside the chip are billions
of tiny parts called

6
00:00:16,050 --> 00:00:16,850
transistors.

7
00:00:17,750 --> 00:00:21,630
Each one holds a single
answer, like a yes or

8
00:00:21,630 --> 00:00:22,430
a no.

9
00:00:23,050 --> 00:00:25,410
Eight of them in a row
can stand for any one

10
00:00:25,410 --> 00:00:28,370
of two hundred and fifty-six
things, like a letter,

11
00:00:28,850 --> 00:00:30,270
a colour, or a number.

12
00:00:31,030 --> 00:00:33,910
Line up enough of them, and
you can describe a song,

13
00:00:33,910 --> 00:00:35,370
or a face.

14
00:00:36,210 --> 00:00:38,730
Change them fast enough,
and the picture moves.

15
00:00:39,650 --> 00:00:40,490
So what's the trick?

16
00:00:41,270 --> 00:00:42,910
Each transistor is a switch.

17
00:00:43,830 --> 00:00:46,250
And all your computer can
do is tell whether a switch

18
00:00:46,250 --> 00:00:47,710
is on, or off.
